        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome/Edge desktop 141 add support for the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaDevices/getDisplayMedia\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">getDisplayMedia()</code></a> <code class=\"notranslate\">windowAudio</code> option. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5072779506089984\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5072779506089984</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds support for the new option. Note the slightly weird set of default values that differ across browsers and versions, and the partial implementation. I found these results by testing a modified version of <a href=\"https://mdn.github.io/dom-examples/screen-capture-api/basic-screen-capture/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn.github.io/dom-examples/screen-capture-api/basic-screen-capture/</a> with the new option added in.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
