        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">SpeechRecognition</code> API. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.15.1).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/SpeechRecognition\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/SpeechRecognition</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Additional Notes: This effectively reverts the parts of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3422368538\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27901\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27901/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27901\">#27901</a> that relate to on-device speech recognition.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28112",
            "title": "Update Chromium data for SpeechRecognition API",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-07T12:21:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-07T05:24:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR addresses <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27769#pullrequestreview-3298716689\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27769/hovercard\">feedback provided about method support in <code class=\"notranslate\">sync</code> storage in Firefox for Android</a> by:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>adding note to the methods under <code class=\"notranslate\">StorageArea</code>.</li>\n<li>adding <code class=\"notranslate\">impl_url</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code> properties under <code class=\"notranslate\">sync</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In addition, the support for <code class=\"notranslate\">getBytesInUse</code> under <code class=\"notranslate\">session</code> storage was corrected to indicate the method is not supported (it's not supported anywhere within Firefox for Android.)</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28107",
            "title": "Bug-1625257 sync storage support in Android",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-06T17:51:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-06T17:50:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 141 adds support for the new <code class=\"notranslate\">all</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">remote-only</code> values of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaTrackConstraints/echoCancellation\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MediaTrackConstraints/echoCancellation</code></a> constraint. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5585747985563648\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5585747985563648</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR in particular adds data points for these as sub-values of <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaStreamTrack.applyConstraints()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaStreamTrack.getCapabilities()</code>. The former is used as the data for the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaTrackConstraints</code> pages, but the latter is used to query the platform for constraint support, and I'm pretty sure it must be available there too.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
